+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01: notification markup escaping
+
+- [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go:formatSlowUpstreamBody` and `desktop.go:Handler.writeProcessChain` both render the process chain with " ← " (the slow-upstream comment says "matching desktop.go"). They differ in the leading newline and PIDs. Make one `markup` method that both call.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:searchAttrsText` and `internal/cli/format.go:formatAttrs` both render search attributes as "k=v, k=v"; the CLI copy is unsorted. Move one sorted formatter into `approval` and use it in both.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go`: the SSH `"destination"` attribute key is written in `sshagent/proxy.go:73` and read here. Give it one named constant (or a typed field on the request).
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:46`: the `Action` doc says "approve" or "deny", but six action keys exist, and the key literals are split between `sendNotification`/`handleCancelled` and `handleAction`. Use typed constants.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:161-236`: "retry once after reconnect on ErrClosed" is written three times (Notify, NotifyPersistent, Close). Extract one helper. The urgency `2` appears four times as a magic number.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:310,513-523`: `cancelledRequests` is written and pruned but never read. Delete it, or wire up the auto-approve lookup it was meant for. Its 5-minute expiry is stated in a comment and in the literal.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:326`: `NewHandler` takes six parameters, with two adjacent `time.Duration`s. Use an options struct.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go` and `desktop_test.go`: about 25 doc comments open with their declaration's own name. The test file's `contains`/`stringContains` reimplement `strings.Contains`.
+- [ ] Notification bodies are sent as markup without checking the server's `body-markup` capability. A server without it shows `&lt;` literally.
